Backstage Coding modified the compilation by retaining bounded factual fields,
joining exact IDs, separating reward choices, and omitting narrative descriptions,
personal data and undocumented prerequisite correlations. Each build is normalized
separately, then merged newest-first: quest givers, turn-ins, objective positions
and NPC positions are unioned with exact dedupe and bounded caps, and scalar facts
(titles, levels, links, rewards) come from the newest build that reports them.
NPC window positions are approximate player observation positions, not guaranteed
creature spawns. Per-record sources counts contributing saved files (the largest
single-build count), not observation counts.
